      "parent_ids": [
        "9c139e4db0c7d09109ee4e212d6cbde0419a745c"
      ],
      "title": "PTP: Fixing TLV Parsing",
      "message": "PTP: Fixing TLV Parsing\n\nThe original code had to many assumptions on TLV handling and was not\nflexible and robust enough.\n\nThis patch refactors the TLV parsing and fixes the following problems:\n- Some messages types did not allow for multiple TLVs\n- Assumptions on which TLVs could be present lead to issues\n- Assumptions on TLV ordering lead to issues\n- TLVs were parsed based on assumptions instead of IDs/Types\n- TLV parsing was not robust\n- TLV parsing had a lot of undissected byte warnings (reserved, etc.)\n- Filters for tlvType, etc. depended on message they were attached to\n\nTLV parsing is now much more flexible. Instead of limiting parsing,\nexpert info is being added to show mistakes, so that malformed messages\ncan be analyzed.\n\nAlso, the TLV parsing does not use absolute offsets anymore but uses\nrelative positioning, which leads to much more robust parsing and would\nhave avoided past bugs of this dissector.\n\nAdded support to call a subdissector for TLVs.\n\nAdded the missing CSN TLV too.\n",
      "author_name": "Dr. Lars Völker",
      "author_email": "lars.voelker@technica-engineering.de",
      "authored_date": "2024-12-09T15:06:50.000+01:00",
      "committer_name": "Alexis La Goutte",
      "committer_email": "alexis.lagoutte@gmail.com",
